  - id: about
    heading: about
    info: 'Enjoy the thrill of blackjack anytime, anywhere with our online game.
      Immerse yourself in realistic graphics, user-friendly interface, and secure
      play.

      Key Points.



      1. Realistic graphics.

      2. User-friendly
      interface.

      3. Secure play.

      4.Convenient access anytime.

      5.
      Thrilling blackjack experience.



      <b><size=90>About Us</size><b>



      Welcome
      to PB Blackjack, your premier destination for an immersive online Blackjack
      experience!

      At PB Blackjack, we''re committed to delivering an authentic
      and thrilling gaming environment where players can enjoy the classic game of
      Blackjack from the comfort of their own home. Our platform boasts sleek and
      intuitive design, ensuring seamless gameplay for both novice and seasoned players
      alike.

      What sets PB Blackjack apart is our dedication to fair play and
      transparency. We prioritise security measures to safeguard our players'' information
      and provide a secure gaming environment. Additionally, our platform offers
      a wide range of customizable options, allowing players to tailor their gaming
      experience to their preferences.

      Whether you''re a casual player looking
      for some entertainment or a serious gambler seeking a challenge, PB Blackjack
      has something for everyone. Join us today and experience the excitement of
      Blackjack like never before!

      Remember, while Blackjack is a game of
      skill and strategy, it''s also about having fun responsibly. Play smart, know
      your limits, and most importantly, enjoy the thrill of the game!

'
  - id: rules
    heading: rules
    info: "<b><size=90>Objective :</size><b> The goal of Blackjack is to beat the
      dealer's hand without going over 21.\n\n<b><size=90>Card Values :</size><b>
      Numbered cards (2-10) are worth their face value. Face cards (Jack, Queen,
      King) are worth 10 points each. Aces can be worth either 1 or 11 points, depending
      on which value benefits the player's hand.\n\n\n<b><size=90>The Deal :</size><b>
      Each player is dealt two cards face up, while the dealer receives one card
      face up and one card face down (the hole card).\n\n\n<b><size=90>Player's Turn
      :</size><b> Players have the option \n\n* <size=70>Hit :</size> Request an
      additional card. You can hit as many times as you like, but if the total value
      exceeds 21, you \"bust\" and lose the game.\n\n* <size=70>Stand :</size> Keep
      your current hand and end your turn.\n\n* <size=70>Double Down :</size> Double
      your original bet, receive one additional card, and then automatically stand.\n\n*
      <size=70>Split :</size> If you have two cards of the same value, you can split
      them into two separate hands and play each hand individually. You must place
      an additional bet equal to your original wager.\n\n* <size=70>Surrender :</size>
      Some casinos allow players to forfeit half their bet and end the round immediately.
      This is called \"surrender.\"\n\n\n<b><size=90>Dealer's Turn :</size><b> After
      all players have completed their turns, the dealer reveals the hole card. The
      dealer must hit until their hand reaches a total of 17 or higher.\n\n\n<b><size=90>Winning
      :</size><b> Players win if their hand is closer to 21 than the dealer's hand
      without going over 21. If the player's hand exceeds 21, they bust and lose
      the round. If the dealer busts and the player doesn't, the player wins. If
      the player and dealer tie, it's called a push, and the player's bet is returned.\n\n\n<b><size=90>Blackjack
      :</size><b> If a player's first two cards are an Ace and a 10-point card (10,
      Jack, Queen, King), they have a Blackjack, and typically win 1.5 times their
      bet unless the dealer also has a Blackjack, resulting in a push.\n"
